diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 49375d41c..b3fb1900a 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -312,7 +312,7 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 - **Free window:** during the first ~75 turns at Normal speed (scaled by game speed), a "free to produce settler" period lets the capital grow before switching into chosen early strategy (offense, defense, etc.).
 - **First city logic:** settlers consider a larger no-penalty scouting radius for founding the capital (`CvUnitAI::AI_foundFirstCity`), and no longer auto-reject non-coastal/non-river sites if a worse "preferred" site exists. It’ll just pick the **best** overall site. See [KI#43](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#43---attemptingly-improvedenhanced-ai-settlers-for-the-first-city-found-ie-at-turn-0-if-i-am-not-mistaken-settling-too-soon-instead-of-digging-a-bit-for-better-sites-and-other-related-changes).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5940+) **First-city roaming**: Since the first city is especially important, unlike later cities that can be more strategic or semi-decent resource grabs, starting settlers can now **roam briefly for a better first-city site when the current site is bad enough**. Settlers can spend the bounded early window to **move to visible good-enough sites**, do **safe adjacent scouting for better information**, or **wait if no safe scouting step exists**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5976+) Starting-site checks use a shared **potential-food environment score** (using the same logic described under Low-food environments). Food-surplus plots offset poor plots, productive Grass Hills remain neutral, and no-yield peaks/ice receive an extra citizen-unworkable penalty because they are dead BFC slots. This keeps useful resources/coasts from looking poor while still moving away from bad tundra/plains/peak-heavy starts.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5940+) **First-city recheck after scouting**: **instead of settling the first good-enough** capital site found **after leaving a very bad start**, the **settler now runs first-city evaluation again** on **nearby visible plots** including **now newly visible** ones first, like a human player would. Empirically, this helped choose even stronger nearby capital sites with more usable food bonuses and/or river support rather than stopping at the first merely-no-longer-bad site. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6008+) Recovery candidates must now have a fully revealed BFC before interrupting bounded scouting; when the scouting window ends, the settler rechecks revealed reachable sites instead of blindly founding wherever scouting stopped. This prevents partially known sites from prematurely ending information gathering and prevents the final scouting tile from becoming the capital by accident. As of now this applies only to the first city, because as of now only the first city is deemed most needing it critically, and later settlers usually know more of the local map so they would generally have a lower need to change route midway (may create other issues too maybe). See [KI#144](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#144---fixed-base-advciv-issue-and-advciv-sas-settler-free-window-follow-up-ai-settlers-sometimes-do-not-move-away-from-a-high-bad-plot-count-start-eg-high-non-bonus-tundra-and-plains-they-now-scout-and-hunt-for-better-not-very-bad-sites-and-no-longer-stop-at-first-good-enough-site-but-instead-now-rerun-evaluate-city-site-again-on-newly-visible-plots-if-a-better-site-eg-more-foodriversfresh-water-exists-nearby-which-we-now-value-more-too-for-first-city-as-well).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6009+) **First-city recheck and efficient return after scouting:** After leaving a very poor spawn location, the AI settler explores nearby unrevealed plots (fog) within a limited scouting window (in turns) instead of founding the first merely good-enough site, trying to find better first-city sites, like a human player would. Only fully revealed BFCs can interrupt scouting; before each further step, the AI settler compares its current plot and other revealed reachable sites by full city-site value minus a tunable return-path cost. The turns window includes the trip back, so the AI settler commits before further scouting would make its best return too late, then queues movement and founding together instead of restarting scouting on arrival or founding wherever scouting stopped. Empirically and as BBAI logging also showed, this helped Berlin, Karakorum, Cuzco, and the Aztecs choose strong revealed sites and found promptly in save files 442, 360, and 431. As of now this applies only to the first city, which critically benefits from extra information and founds much stronger first-city sites, while later AI settlers usually know more of the local map and so do not need to use this (so as of now disabled for them). See [KI#144](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#144---fixed-base-advciv-issue-and-advciv-sas-settler-free-window-follow-up-ai-settlers-sometimes-do-not-move-away-from-a-high-bad-plot-count-start-eg-high-non-bonus-tundra-and-plains-they-now-scout-and-hunt-for-better-not-very-bad-sites-and-no-longer-stop-at-first-good-enough-site-but-instead-now-rerun-evaluate-city-site-again-on-newly-visible-plots-if-a-better-site-eg-more-foodriversfresh-water-exists-nearby-which-we-now-value-more-too-for-first-city-as-well).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5928+) **Naval-heavy-map coastal settling:** On naval-heavy (e.g., Archipelago) maps, settler AI site valuation now optionally add **extra valuation for coastal sites**, as of now especially for the **first city**. This helps early work boat, scouting/contact, trade, first galleys, Moai, or other water-focused buildings; e.g., Cuzco needed a high first-city coastal extra valuation to prefer a coastal Pig + Banana + 2-Sugar river site over a central 4-Sugar river grass site; and kept **moderate for other cities** than the capital after testing showed higher values could, for example, overpull Japan toward tundra coast instead of grass. See [KI#146](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#146---fixedenhanced-base-advciv-issue-of-ai-undervaluing-coastal-settling-on-naval-heavy-maps).
 - **Parking addressed (early game):** Reduced cases of settlers idling in the capital despite safe/urgent expansion, by updating `CvUnitAI::AI_found` to found sooner when conditions allow. In autoplay samples, Spain shifted from **1 city @T100** to **~2 by T60–70** and **~3 by T80–90** (settler production varies somehow, but we move much sooner after we have it now). See [KI#68](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#68---tremendously-improved-ai-having-a-settler-parked-from-turn---45-to-turn-100-and-still-didnt-found-any-city-fixedaddressed-in-cvunitaiai_found).

